      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 108358730,
      "text": "ナンヨウソテツ はソテツ科ソテツ属の雌雄異株の常緑樹。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Cycas rumphii",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycas_rumphii",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1330651777,
      "text": "Cycas rumphii, commonly known as queen sago or the queen sago palm, is a dioecious gymnosperm, a species of cycad in the genus Cycas native to Indonesia, New Guinea and Christmas Island. Although palm-like in appearance, it is not a palm."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Cycas rumphii",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycas_rumphii",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 224828796,
      "text": "Cycas rumphii est une espèce de plantes de la famille des Cycadaceae."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Cycas rumphii",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycas_rumphii",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 54754828,
      "text": "Cycas rumphii é uma espécie de cicadófita do género Cycas da família Cycadaceae, nativa da China (possívelmente), Sri Lanka, Indonésia, Malásia, Papua-Nova Guiné, Guão, Fiji, Nova Caledónia e Ilhas Salomão. Esta espécie tem importância ornamental e dela é extraído amido usado na alimentação humana. Segundo dados de 2010, a população tende a descrescer."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Cycas rumphii",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycas_rumphii",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 26598535,
      "text": "Cycas rumphii adalah salah satu jenis pakis haji (Cycas) yang umum ditemukan di Nusantara. Tumbuhan ini asli berasal dari kepulauan ini dan apabila orang menyebut \"pakis haji\", maka yang dimaksud biasanya adalah C. rumphii ini. Tumbuhan ini biasa ditanam orang sebagai penghias pekarangan rumah dan batangnya mengandung pati yang dapat dimakan."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "ja": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (ja): ナンヨウソテツ § 利用",
        "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%8A%E3%83%B3%E3%83%A8%E3%82%A6%E3%82%BD%E3%83%86%E3%83%84#%E5%88%A9%E7%94%A8",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 108358730,
        "heading": "利用",
        "text": "観葉植物として利用。\n種子や幹はソテツと同様に澱粉を含み、原産地ではこれを水洗いして食用にするが、有毒成分による中毒事故も起きていたとされる。若葉を食用にするとも記される。",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Cycas rumphii § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycas_rumphii#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1330651777,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "The trunk of the cycad contains a starchy pith from which sago can be prepared by drying, grinding and washing. The seeds contain a toxic glucoside, pakoein, but can be treated to become edible by pounding, repeated washing, and cooking. The bark, seeds and sap are used in poultices to treat sores. Called Namwele in the Kastom culture of Pentecost, Vanuatu, the plant is sacred, a symbol of peace and status.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
